{
 "_source": "base\\gameplay\\devices\\masters\\computers\\computer_1.ent as vanilla places it in quest_73110a178d6e7404.streamingsector, node 12 - a worldEntityNode with appearance computer_computer_2_angle_15, which is the same .ent, the same node type and the same appearance this quest places. Extracted verbatim by tools, not typed by hand.",
 "_why": [
  "OI-13 asked whether a DEVICE can be placed with instanceData null, the way",
  "base\\entities\\covers\\left_sided_low_cover.ent is. The probe node",
  "ac_probe_computer was placed with null to find out, and world.json wrote the",
  "test down before it was run: 'If it appears AND can be interacted with,",
  "terminal_read, box_opened and cabinet_opened are all cheap. If it appears",
  "but is inert, they need the buffer.'",
  "",
  "The player reported it on 2026-09-09: it appears, drawn as a bare screen",
  "plane, and there is no interaction on it at all. So: they need the buffer.",
  "This is the buffer. isInteractive is 1 and tweakDBRecord is Devices.Computer;",
  "with no instanceData there is no ComputerControllerPS at all, so there is",
  "nothing to be interactive and no device record to draw a body from."
 ],
 "_handleids": "The 12 HandleIds in here (24-35 as vanilla numbered them) are definitions - each appears exactly once and nothing references them - so gen_sector.py renumbers them per node. Two props carrying this buffer would otherwise define the same handle twice in one file.",
 "_cruid": "CruidDict is copied unchanged, deliberately. It is NOT a per-node unique id: nodes 79, 80 and 84 of quest_e495c59e9949e75b all carry the same 3609005567401009152, and 1508365491801698304 appears in two different sectors. Vanilla duplicates it across identical placements, so duplicating it is what matching vanilla means (rule 8).",
